hadiths[50]{hadithnumber,text}:
"260","It is narrated on the authority of Hadrat Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \I swear by that Being in whose Hand is my soul"," you shall not enter Paradise until you bring faith"," and you shall not truly believe until you love one another. Shall I not direct you to something that"," if you act upon it"," you will love one another? Spread salām (greetings of peace) amongst yourselves"," and you will love one another. And beware of hatred and enmity"," for it is the shaver. I do not say that it shaves hair"," but rather it shaves away the religion.\"" A similar narration is also reported through another chain of narration from Ibrahim bin Usaid.\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 260*"""
"261","It is narrated on the authority of Hadrat Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Indeed"," the souls of two believers meet each other at a distance of a day's journey"," even though one of them has never seen the other.\""\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 261*"""
"262","It is narrated on the authority of Hadrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: \Blessings are shown ingratitude"," mercy is severed"," and I have not seen any bond of affection comparable to the closeness of hearts.\""\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 262*"""
"263","Umair bin Ishaq (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \We used to say that among people"," the first thing to be taken away will be intimacy and affection.\""\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 263*"""
"264","It is narrated on the authority of Hadrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to some of his wives, and Umm Sulaim (may Allah be pleased with her) was also among them. He said: \O Unaisah! Take the bottles away gently.\"" The narrator"," Abu Qilabah"," said: \""The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this instruction so that if anyone among you were to say something"," you would not take it in an unpleasant sense. What I mean by the Prophet's words is: 'Handle the glass vessels with care.'\""\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 264*"""
"265","It is narrated on the authority of Hadrat Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \O Messenger of Allah! You joke with us!\"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Indeed"," whatever I speak (even in jest) is the truth.\""\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 265*"""
"266","It is narrated on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah (may Allah have mercy upon him). He said: \The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to throw watermelons at one another in jest"," but when matters of truth arose — such as matters of honour and defence — they were truly men of valour.\""\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 266*"""
"267","It is narrated on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaikah (may Allah have mercy upon him) that once Hadrat Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said something humorous in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whereupon her mother said: \O Messenger of Allah! (Do not take offence;) several humorous expressions have come to this tribe from Banu Kinanah.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Rather"," some of our humour also belongs to that tribe.\""\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 267*"""
"268","It is narrated on the authority of Hadrat Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that a person requested the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a mount. He said: \I shall have you mounted on a young she-camel.\"" The man said: \""O Messenger of Allah! What shall I do with a young she-camel?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Are camels born from anything other than she-camels?\""\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 268*"""
"269","It is narrated on the authority of Hadrat Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to mingle and play with us"," to the extent that he would say to my younger brother: 'O Abu Umair! What has your little bird done?'\""\n\n*Al-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 269*"""
"270","It is narrated from Hadrat Abu Radhiyallahu 'Anhu that the Prophet Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam took the hand of Sayyidna Hasan or Husayn Radhiyallahu 'Anhuma and placed their feet upon his blessed feet, then said: \Climb up.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 270 | Arabic Hadith: 270"""
"271","It is narrated from Hadrat Abu Darda Radhiyallahu 'Anhu, who relates from the Prophet Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam that he said: \Nothing shall weigh heavier in the Scale (of deeds on the Day of Resurrection) than good character.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 271 | Arabic Hadith: 271"""
"272","It is narrated from Hadrat Abdullah ibn Amr Radhiyallahu 'Anhuma, who said: The Prophet Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam was neither obscene in speech nor did he indulge in obscenity deliberately. Rather, he used to say: \The best among you are those who possess the finest character.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 272 | Arabic Hadith: 272"""
"273","It is narrated from Hadrat Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-'As Radhiyallahu 'Anhuma that he heard the Prophet Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam saying: \Shall I not inform you about the person among you who is most beloved to me and who will be closest to me in assembly on the Day of Resurrection?\"" The people fell silent. He repeated his words two or three times. The people said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah!\"" He said: \""The one among you who possesses the best character.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 273 | Arabic Hadith: 273"""
"274","It is narrated from Hadrat Abu Hurayrah Radhiyallahu 'Anhu that the Messenger of Allah Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam said: \I was sent solely for the perfection of noble character.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 274 | Arabic Hadith: 274"""
"275","It is narrated from Hadrat 'A'ishah Radhiyallahu 'Anha, who said: Whenever the Prophet Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam was given a choice between two matters, he would choose the easier of the two, so long as it was not a sinful act. If it were a sinful act, he would be the furthest of all people from it. And the Messenger of Allah Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam never took vengeance for himself, except when the sanctities of Allah were violated, in which case he would take vengeance for the sake of Allah the Almighty.\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad, Hadith: 275 | Arabic Hadith: 275"
"276","It is narrated from Hadrat Abdullah ibn Mas'ud Radhiyallahu 'Anhu that he said: Indeed, Allah the Most High has distributed character among you just as He has distributed provision among you. Verily, Allah the Most High grants wealth to whomever He wills and to whomever He does not will, and He grants faith only to those whom He loves. The one who is miserly in spending, fears fighting the enemy, and lacks the resolve to stand in prayer during the night, let him abundantly recite 'La ilaha illallah,' 'SubhanAllah,' 'Alhamdulillah,' and 'Allahu Akbar.'\\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 276 | Arabic Hadith: 276"""
"277","It is narrated from Hadrat Abu Hurayrah Radhiyallahu 'Anhu, who relates from the Prophet Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam that he said: \Wealth is not an abundance of worldly possessions; rather"," true wealth is the wealth of the soul.\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 277 | Arabic Hadith: 277"""
"278","It is narrated from Hadrat Anas ibn Malik Radhiyallahu 'Anhu that he said: I served the Prophet Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam for ten years, yet he never said \Uff\"" to me"," and whenever I failed to do something"," he never said"," \""Why did you not do it?\"" Nor did it ever happen that I did something and he said"," \""Why did you do it?\""\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 278 | Arabic Hadith: 278"""
"279","It is narrated from Hadrat Anas ibn Malik Radhiyallahu 'Anhu that the Prophet Sallallahu 'Alayhi Wasallam was exceedingly merciful and compassionate. Whenever a beggar came to him (and he had nothing to give), he would make a promise to him, and if he had something, he would certainly give it. Once, the Iqamah for prayer was announced when a bedouin came to him, grabbed his cloak, and said: \I have a small matter remaining; I fear I may forget it"," so please listen to what I have to say.\"" He stood with him until the man had finished speaking"," and then he came and led the prayer.\nAl-Adab Al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 279 | Arabic Hadith: 279"""
"280","It is narrated from Jābir (may Allāh be pleased with him) that whatever he was asked about in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him), he never said \no.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 280 | Arabic Hadith: 280"""
"281","It is narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Zubayr (may Allāh be pleased with them both), who said: \I have not seen any woman more generous than ʿĀʾishah and Asmāʾ (may Allāh be pleased with them both)"," and the nature of their generosity was distinct. ʿĀʾishah (may Allāh be pleased with her) would accumulate wealth"," and when she had gathered some"," she would spend it all. Asmāʾ (may Allāh be pleased with her)"," on the other hand"," would not save anything for the morrow — whatever came to her"," she would spend.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 281 | Arabic Hadith: 281"""
"282","It is narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) said: \The dust that settles in the stomach of a servant in the path of Allāh and the smoke of Hell shall never come together. Likewise"," miserliness and faith shall never coexist in the heart of a servant.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 282 | Arabic Hadith: 282"""
"283","It is narrated from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) said: \Two qualities cannot coexist in a believer: miserliness and bad character.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 283 | Arabic Hadith: 283"""
"284","It is narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabīʿah (may Allāh have mercy on him) that we were in the presence of Sayyidunā ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allāh be pleased with him) when he mentioned a man and also spoke of his character. Sayyidunā ʿAbdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \Tell me"," if you were to cut off his head"," could you rejoin it?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then his hand?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then his leg?\"" They said: \""No.\"" Ibn Masʿūd (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \""Since you cannot alter his physical creation"," you likewise cannot alter his character. Indeed"," the drop of semen remains in the womb for forty nights"," then it takes the form of a clot of blood"," then it becomes a clinging lump (ʿalaqah)"," then it becomes a lump of flesh (muḍghah)"," and then Allāh"," the Most High"," sends an angel who records his provision"," his character"," and whether he is wretched or blessed.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 284 | Arabic Hadith: 284"""
"285","It is narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) said: \Indeed"," a person attains the rank of one who stands in prayer throughout the night by virtue of his good character.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 285 | Arabic Hadith: 285"""
"286","It is narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) that I heard Abū al-Qāsim (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) say: \The best of you in terms of Islam are those whose character is the finest"," provided they also possess understanding of the religion.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 286 | Arabic Hadith: 286"""
"287","Thābit ibn ʿUbayd (may Allāh have mercy on him) said: \I have not seen a man more dignified in gatherings of friends and more cheerful in his home than Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allāh be pleased with him).\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 287 | Arabic Hadith: 287"""
"288","It is narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) was asked: \Which religion is most beloved to Allāh"," the Mighty and Majestic?\"" He said: \""Al-Ḥanīfiyyah — the upright and easy way.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 288 | Arabic Hadith: 288"""
"289","It is narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allāh be pleased with them both), who said: \If four things are granted to you"," then no loss can befall you even if the rest of the world's provisions pass you by: good character"," eating from what is ḥalāl"," truthfulness in speech"," and the safeguarding of trusts.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 289 | Arabic Hadith: 289"""
"290","It is narrated from Hadrat Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Do you know what will cause the majority of people to enter the Fire?\"" The people said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""Two hollow things: the private parts and the mouth. And what will cause the majority of people to enter Paradise is taqwa (consciousness of Allah) and good character.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 290*"""
"291","It is narrated from Hadrat Umm Darda (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: Hadrat Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) would rise at night for prayer and begin weeping, saying: \O Allah"," You have made my appearance beautiful"," so make my character beautiful as well.\"" He continued making this supplication until morning. I said: \""O Abu Darda! You have spent the entire night making supplication solely for good character.\"" He said: \""O Umm Darda! If a Muslim's character is good"," it will admit him into Paradise"," and if his character is bad"," it will admit him into the Fire. And when a Muslim servant is asleep"," he is forgiven.\"" I said: \""O Abu Darda! How is the one who is asleep forgiven?\"" He said: \""His brother rises at night to pray Tahajjud and then supplicates to Allah"," the Exalted"," and his supplication is accepted. And he supplicates for his brother"," and the supplication he makes concerning his brother is also accepted.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 291*"""
"292","It is narrated from Hadrat Usamah ibn Sharik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the Hajj, and the Bedouins came — many people from this side and many from that side. The people fell silent, and no one else was speaking. They said: \O Messenger of Allah! Is there any sin in doing such and such?\"" They mentioned many matters in which there was no harm. He said: \""Allah"," the Exalted"," has removed hardship and restriction. However"," whoever unjustly consumes the flesh of another"," he remains in hardship and is destroyed.\"" They asked: \""O Messenger of Allah! May we use medicine?\"" He said: \""O servants of Allah! Seek treatment"," for indeed Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has sent down a cure for every disease except one.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah! What is that disease?\"" He said: \""Old age.\"" They asked: \""O Messenger of Allah! What is the best and finest thing that has been bestowed upon a person?\"" He said: \""Good character.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 292*"""
"293","It is narrated from Hadrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most generous of all people, and he was at his most generous during Ramadan when Jibril (peace be upon him) would meet him. Jibril (peace be upon him) would meet him every night of Ramadan and review the Quran with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And when Jibril met him, he was even more generous than the blowing wind.\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 293*"
"294","It is narrated from Hadrat Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \A man from among those who came before you was brought to account"," and nothing was found in his record of deeds except that he used to mix with people and was wealthy"," and he would instruct his servants and employees to overlook the debts of those in difficulty. Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: 'We have more right to that (forgiveness and pardon)","' and so He forgave him.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 294*"""
"295","It is narrated from Hadrat Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that it was asked of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \What will cause the most people to enter Paradise?\"" He said: \""Taqwa (consciousness of Allah) and good character.\"" The questioner asked: \""What will cause the most people to enter the Hellfire?\"" He said: \""Two hollow things: the mouth and the private parts.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 295*"""
"296","It is narrated from Hadrat an-Nawwas ibn Sam'an al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about righteousness and sin. He said: \Righteousness is good character"," and sin is that which pricks your chest and which you dislike people coming to know about.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 296*"""
"297","It is narrated from Hadrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \O Banu Salamah! Who is your chief?\"" We said: \""Jud ibn Qays"," although we consider him to be miserly.\"" He said: \""Is there any disease worse than miserliness? Rather"," your chief is Amr ibn al-Jumuh.\"" And Amr ibn al-Jumuh used to be the custodian of their idols during the Age of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah). Later"," when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would marry"," he would arrange the wedding feast on his behalf.\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 297*"""
"298","It is narrated from Warrad, the secretary of Hadrat Mughirah (may Allah be pleased with him), that Hadrat Mu'awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote a letter to Mughirah ibn Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: \Write to me any hadith that you have heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).\"" So Hadrat Mughirah ibn Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid idle talk"," the squandering of wealth"," and excessive questioning. He also used to forbid withholding and then demanding expenditure from others"," disobedience to mothers"," and the burying of daughters alive.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 298*"""
"299","It is narrated from Hadrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that whenever anything was requested from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he never said: \I will not give.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 299*"""
"300","It is narrated by ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to come to him wearing my battle attire and bearing arms. I did so accordingly. When I arrived in his presence"," he was performing ablution. He raised his gaze toward me and then lowered his head. Then he said: 'O ʿAmr! I wish to appoint you as the commander of an army and send you forth"," and may Allah grant you war booty. I desire good wealth for you.' I submitted: 'I did not embrace Islam out of desire for wealth. I embraced Islam solely out of love for the religion of Islam"," so that I may have the honour of being in the company of the Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'O ʿAmr! Good wealth is a fine provision for a righteous man.'\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 300 | Arabic Hadith: 300"""
"301","It is narrated by ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muḥsin al-Anṣārī (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: \Whoever wakes up in the morning in a state wherein he feels secure regarding himself and his family"," is in good physical health"," and has with him a day's provision of food"," it is as though the entire world has been placed at his disposal.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 301 | Arabic Hadith: 301"""
"302","It is narrated by ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥayy (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them, and upon him were the traces of bathing, and he was in a state of great cheerfulness. We assumed that he had been intimate with his wife, so we said: \O Messenger of Allah! You appear exceedingly joyful today.\"" He said: \""All praise is due to Allah"," indeed it is so.\"" Then the topic of wealth and prosperity arose"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""There is no harm in wealth accompanied by taqwā (God-consciousness)"," and for the God-fearing person"," good health is better than wealth"," and a contented soul is among the bounties of Allah.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 302 | Arabic Hadith: 302"""
"303","It is narrated by al-Nawwās ibn Samʿān al-Anṣārī (may Allah be pleased with him) that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning birr (righteousness) and ithm (sin), whereupon he said: \Birr is good character"," and ithm is that which pricks within your breast and you dislike that people should come to know of it.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 303 | Arabic Hadith: 303"""
"304","It is narrated by Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most handsome of all people, the most generous of all people, and the most courageous of all people. One night the people of Madīnah were alarmed, so they set out toward the direction of the sound. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was seen coming from the opposite direction; he had gone ahead of all the people alone toward the source from which the sound had come, saying: \There is nothing to fear; do not be alarmed.\"" He was mounted on the horse of Abū Ṭalḥah without a saddle"," and a sword was hanging around his neck. Then he said: \""I found this horse to be (swift as) a sea","\"" or he said: \""It is certainly a sea (in its speed).\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 304 | Arabic Hadith: 304"""
"305","It is narrated by Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Every act of righteousness is a charity (ṣadaqah). And it is also an act of righteousness that you meet your brother with a cheerful face"," and that you pour from your bucket into your brother's vessel — this too is an act of righteousness.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 305 | Arabic Hadith: 305"""
"306","It is narrated by Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: \Which deeds are the best?\"" He said: \""Belief in Allah and striving in His cause.\"" The questioner asked: \""Which slave is best to emancipate?\"" He said: \""The one most valuable and most esteemed by his masters.\"" The questioner said: \""If I am unable to perform certain deeds"," then what should I do?\"" He said: \""Then assist a person who is being ruined"," or do some work for a foolish person.\"" The questioner said: \""And if I am unable to do even that?\"" He said: \""Then refrain from causing harm to people"," for that too is a charity — a charity you bestow upon yourself.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 306 | Arabic Hadith: 306"""
"307","It is narrated by Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: \It is incumbent upon every Muslim to give charity (ṣadaqah) every day.\"" It was submitted: \""What if he is unable to give charity?\"" He said: \""Then let him work with his own hands"," benefiting himself and also giving charity.\"" It was submitted: \""What if he does not have the strength to do so"," or does not do it?\"" He said: \""Then let him assist a helpless person in need.\"" It was submitted: \""What if he does not have the capacity for that either"," or does not do it?\"" He said: \""Then let him enjoin what is good.\"" It was submitted: \""What if he does not have the strength for that either"," or does not do it?\"" He said: \""Then let him refrain from causing harm and evil to people"," for that too is a charity for him.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 307 | Arabic Hadith: 307"""
"308","It is narrated by ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) frequently made this supplication: \O Allah! I ask You for well-being"," chastity"," trustworthiness"," and good character"," and I ask You for contentment with the divine decree.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 308 | Arabic Hadith: 308"""
"309","Salim ibn 'Abdullah said, \I never heard 'Abdullah ever curse anything.\""\nSalim mentioned that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar said"," \""It is not fitting for a\nbeliever to be a curser.\"""""
